+- `flutter analyze` (and directory-wide `dart analyze`) can pass silently without reporting the
+  `app_lints` diagnostics, while analyzing explicit file paths reports them reliably.
+  `scripts/quality/analyze-dart.sh` therefore runs `dart analyze --fatal-infos` on every tracked
+  Dart file under `lib`, `test`, `integration_test` and `pigeons` (generated files and per-flavor
+  Firebase options excluded)
+- Before trusting a clean result, `scripts/quality/verify-lint-plugin.sh` creates a temporary probe
+  (`lib/app_lints_smoke_probe.dart`, git-ignored, never overwrites an existing file, removed on exit)
+  that deliberately calls `debugPrint`, and requires `avoid_debug_print` to be reported. If it is
+  not, the check fails instead of passing silently; try
+  `(cd packages/app_lints && fvm dart pub get)` and re-run
+- `bash scripts/quality/analyze-dart.sh --staged` is what the `pre-commit` hook runs: it analyzes
+  the staged Dart files, escalates to the full analysis when the lint plugin, `analysis_options.yaml`
+  or dependencies are staged, and refuses files that also have unstaged edits (the analyzer reads
+  the working tree, not the index)
+- The same script runs in CI right after the `Static analysis` step of `ci.yml`, `cd.yml`,
+  `deploy-rc.yml` and `deploy-staging.yml`
 - Because `packages/app_lints` is a standalone Dart package, its dependencies are resolved
